{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned1", "translation": "children without children"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned2", "translation": "city without a city"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned3", "translation": "ships without ships"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned4", "translation": "with right mind"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned5", "translation": "with kindly mind"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned6", "translation": "Straight Justice"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned7", "translation": "with kindly mind"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned8", "translation": "Go forth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned9", "translation": "with all the people"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned10", "translation": "countrymen"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-376-2-mentioned11", "translation": "countryman snake"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ the poets use for 'ancient', 'venerable', ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧.974 (everywhere of cities), ⟦4⟧ ⟦5⟧⟦6⟧ (⟦7⟧). There is no doubt about ⟦8⟧; however, for the rhythm a short syllable is missing, and the parallel passage 1006 ⟦9⟧ recommends ⟦10⟧(⟦11⟧), cf. ⟦12⟧ = ⟦13⟧ ⟦14⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned1", "translation": "Ogygian"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned2", "translation": "power"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned3", "translation": "much-revered"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned4", "translation": "under these august sacrificial victims"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned5", "translation": "much-revered"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned6", "translation": "si"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned7", "translation": "well-revered"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-mentioned8", "translation": "well-revering"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-1-quote1", "translation": "(from Phlius under the Ogygian mountains)"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ = ⟦2⟧ (⟦3⟧ 93)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-2-mentioned1", "translation": "Fortune"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-2-mentioned2", "translation": "with good fortune"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-2-mentioned3", "translation": "with favorable fortune"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (f g h) is to be written, since the length of the ending ⟦2⟧ is present (there also M -⟦3⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-3-mentioned1", "translation": "with all the people"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-377-3-mentioned2", "translation": "ei"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as in Homer A 583 etc.; in Aeschylus only here; Sophocles has ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧, like ⟦4⟧ etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-1-mentioned1", "translation": "propitious"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-1-mentioned2", "translation": "propitious"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-2-comment1", "translation": "For ⟦1⟧ Meineke would like ⟦2⟧, with somewhat too much violence; ⟦3⟧ is nevertheless not inappropriate and corresponds to the disposition shown by the Athenians, 1034."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-2-mentioned1", "translation": "right-minded toward the land"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-2-mentioned2", "translation": "kindly-minded lands"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-2-mentioned3", "translation": "thinking just things toward the land"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-3-comment1", "translation": "At line 1039 the Attic cult name ⟦1⟧ appears (see already 383)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-378-3-mentioned1", "translation": "August Goddesses"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-comment1", "translation": "At 1042 M first had ⟦1⟧, corresponding to the ⟦2⟧ of the antistrophe; ⟦3⟧ Schömann well conjectures (⟦4⟧); Paley keeps ⟦5⟧ and seeks to connect it in meaning with 387. The admonition of the refrain to the ⟦6⟧ (⟦7⟧, ⟦8⟧, ⟦9⟧. 595) is surely again addressed to the people, and specifically to the women, whose business this always is. ⟦10⟧ ⟦11⟧. . ⟦12⟧; so this too is a kind of the ⟦13⟧ (1035)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned1", "translation": "torches"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned2", "translation": "thus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned3", "translation": "pine torch"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned4", "translation": "torch"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned5", "translation": "ritual cry"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned6", "translation": "uttering auspicious sounds"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-mentioned7", "translation": "to speak auspiciously"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-379-1-quote1", "translation": "ritual cry"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-380-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as at 325."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-380-1-mentioned1", "translation": "Upon"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: Athena said at 895, and at 897 ⟦2⟧; so ⟦3⟧ fits with that, and also ⟦4⟧; for even if wine was not poured to the Eumenides, they still received libations of water and ⟦5⟧. Schol. ⟦6⟧: ⟦7⟧, ⟦8⟧ (Phot. ⟦9⟧· ⟦10⟧, ⟦11⟧, Paley on line 107). Now we can connect line 1044 to 1042, with the refrain interrupting the construction just as at 1035, and write ⟦12⟧ or ⟦13⟧, but for ⟦14⟧"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned1", "translation": "So that no house may prosper without you"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned2", "translation": "for to the one who reveres you we will set right misfortunes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned3", "translation": "for the citizens of the house of Pallas"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned4", "translation": "libations"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned5", "translation": "honey-mixture"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned6", "translation": "and their libations are called wineless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned7", "translation": "wineless sacrifices"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned8", "translation": "in which wine is not poured"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned9", "translation": "but water and honey-mixture"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned10", "translation": "with libation"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned11", "translation": "with libations"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-mentioned12", "translation": "torch-bearing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-381-1-quote1", "translation": "for wine is not poured to them, but water"}]}